{"id":"bcce4d16-5258-48b1-b6ea-9c0299a6c1e9","recipient":"9d34f1cc-2595-4c4a-962f-f853c3e22d4e","sender":"b30c3c2b-082b-4dec-9945-1f43ee481e16","priority":"MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH","timestamp":"2026-09-24T19:03:15.370510600Z","renderDetails":{"messageTitle":"Message from UI Agent - Reports & Export Engine (browser)"},"content":"### Browser Agent UI-09: Inspection Report for http://localhost:5173/reports\n\n**Status:** Stopped due to Chrome Connection Failure (Browser Unreachable)\n\nDuring the attempt to inspect `http://localhost:5173/reports` and test the generation of regulatory reports (GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, API Compendium, OGMP 2.0, Algerian National GHG format, date filtering, facility filtering, exports to PDF/CSV/Excel, and UI vs. document totals), the browser tool encountered a connection failure:\n\n```\nCould not connect to Chrome. Check if Chrome is running.\nCause: Could not find DevToolsActivePort for chrome at C:\\Users\\samsung\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\DevToolsActivePort\n```\n\nPer strict connection & safety guidelines, the agent has immediately stopped and cannot launch or spin up Chrome independently.\n\n---\n\n### Troubleshooting Steps Required to Enable Browser Testing:\n\n1. **Check DevToolsActivePort File**:\n   Verify if the file exists at:\n   `C:\\Users\\samsung\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\DevToolsActivePort`\n\n2. **Verify Chrome Remote Debugging**:\n   - Ensure standard Google Chrome is running with remote debugging enabled (e.g. launched with `--remote-debugging-port=<port>`).\n   - Navigate to `chrome://inspect/#remote-debugging` in Chrome and verify the settings.\n\n3. **Check Port Availability & Process Conflicts**:\n   - Verify that the designated debugging port is open and accessible.\n   - Check if multiple Chrome or node processes are listening on or conflicting with the port. If so, terminate conflicting processes.\n\nOnce Chrome is running with remote debugging enabled, please re-invoke Browser Agent UI-09 to proceed with the comprehensive validation of the `/reports` module.\n\n*Note: The recording of this session is available in the conversation artifacts.*","sourceMetadata":{"tool":{"conversationId":"b30c3c2b-082b-4dec-9945-1f43ee481e16","stepIndex":15,"toolCall":{"id":"call_692298","name":"send_message","argumentsJson":"{\"Message\":\"### Browser Agent UI-09: Inspection Report for http://localhost:5173/reports\\n\\n**Status:** Stopped due to Chrome Connection Failure (Browser Unreachable)\\n\\nDuring the attempt to inspect `http://localhost:5173/reports` and test the generation of regulatory reports (GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, API Compendium, OGMP 2.0, Algerian National GHG format, date filtering, facility filtering, exports to PDF/CSV/Excel, and UI vs. document totals), the browser tool encountered a connection failure:\\n\\n```\\nCould not connect to Chrome. Check if Chrome is running.\\nCause: Could not find DevToolsActivePort for chrome at C:\\\\Users\\\\samsung\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Google\\\\Chrome\\\\User Data\\\\DevToolsActivePort\\n```\\n\\nPer strict connection \\u0026 safety guidelines, the agent has immediately stopped and cannot launch or spin up Chrome independently.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Troubleshooting Steps Required to Enable Browser Testing:\\n\\n1. **Check DevToolsActivePort File**:\\n   Verify if the file exists at:\\n   `C:\\\\Users\\\\samsung\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Google\\\\Chrome\\\\User Data\\\\DevToolsActivePort`\\n\\n2. **Verify Chrome Remote Debugging**:\\n   - Ensure standard Google Chrome is running with remote debugging enabled (e.g. launched with `--remote-debugging-port=\\u003cport\\u003e`).\\n   - Navigate to `chrome://inspect/#remote-debugging` in Chrome and verify the settings.\\n\\n3. **Check Port Availability \\u0026 Process Conflicts**:\\n   - Verify that the designated debugging port is open and accessible.\\n   - Check if multiple Chrome or node processes are listening on or conflicting with the port. If so, terminate conflicting processes.\\n\\nOnce Chrome is running with remote debugging enabled, please re-invoke Browser Agent UI-09 to proceed with the comprehensive validation of the `/reports` module.\\n\\n*Note: The recording of this session is available in the conversation artifacts.*\",\"Recipient\":\"9d34f1cc-2595-4c4a-962f-f853c3e22d4e\",\"toolAction\":\"Reporting Chrome connection error\",\"toolSummary\":\"Send connection error report to caller\"}","thinkingSignature":""}}}}